       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 4000 mg four times daily is 16,000 mg/day, which is five times the maximum daily dose of oral ibuprofen for adults. That maximum is 3,200 mg/day under medical supervision, and 1,200 mg/day for over-the-counter use. A dose that high risks serious GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular and CNS toxicity.\n\nThis may be a typo for 400 mg. Typical regimens are:\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day), which is common for pain or inflammation.\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), which is the usual maximum for chronic use.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 4000 mg per dose, please confirm that explicitly and give the clinical rationale for the order note."
