     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 4000 mg per dose is 16,000 mg/day. No indication supports that dose, and it is in the range where serious toxicity is expected (GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, metabolic acidosis, CNS depression, seizures). Entering it as written could seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Typo:** If you meant 400 mg, I can enter 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day) right now. I can also enter 600 mg four times daily or 800 mg three times daily if you prefer.\n- **Higher anti-inflammatory dosing:** For a specific indication such as rheumatologic disease, I can enter up to 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day), or up to 3,200 mg/day in divided doses. That is the labeled ceiling.\n- **Dose above the labeled maximum:** If you think the patient needs more than that, please talk to pharmacy or the attending first. I'd also look at a different drug, because NSAIDs have a ceiling effect for analgesia.\n\nTell me which dose you want, and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
